OL,3,GNEWSANo plans to scrap minimum wage,
OL,4,Asays chief minister
OL,5,
OL,6,FJersey's chief minister says the
OL,7,Fgovernment has "no plans" to abolish
OL,8,Fthe island's minimum wage, set at
OL,9,F#13.59 an hour.
OL,11,FSenator Lyndon Farnham was responding
OL,12,Fto a letter in the Jersey Evening Post
OL,13,Ffrom the Sustainable Economic
OL,14,FDevelopment Minister Gerald Voisin who
OL,15,Fsaid the minimum wage was "strangling
OL,16,Four economy".
OL,23,APub: 18-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
